Lesson (stxt.play.tutorial): Namespace documents
	Number of lesson: 5/5
	Introduction >>
		Documents with a namespace have
		nodes of this form: `Node name (namespace.definition):`
		or `Node name (namespace.definition) >>`

		From this lesson on, all
		the documents have a namespace.

		Nodes with a namespace can be validated against schemas.
		The schema gives the structure and the cardinality
		of the children.

		The parser can be configured with or without validation.
		This workspace has a switch to enable or disable
		schema validation.

		Next, you can play with a recipe: change it
		and see what happens with validation.

Recipe (stxt.play.cooking): Spaghetti bolognese
	Ingredients:
		Ingredient: 400 g spaghetti
		Ingredient: 400 g minced beef
		Ingredient: 400 g crushed tomatoes
		Ingredient: Olive oil, salt and oregano
		Ingredient: Grated cheese
	Steps >>
		Brown the mince. Add the tomatoes, salt and oregano and simmer for half an hour.
		Boil the pasta, drain it, mix with the sauce and top with grated cheese.
	Notes >>
		The sauce is **better the next day**, so make it ahead if you can.
		Some people finish it in the oven for five minutes to melt the cheese.
